### 1. pitfall: the publisher is shut down while its slot still has unconsumed changes
Checking for valid logical replication slots                  fatal

Your installation contains logical replication slots that cannot be upgraded.
You can remove invalid slots and/or consume the pending WAL for other slots,
and then restart the upgrade.
A list of the problematic slots is in the file:
    /pgdata/p18/pg_upgrade_output.d/20260921T173420.687/invalid_logical_slots.txt
Failure, exiting
[pg_upgrade --check exit status: 1]
invalid_logical_slots.txt says:
The slot "sub" has not consumed the WAL yet

### 2. bring both back so the slot consumes everything, then shut the publisher down again
[5442]> SELECT count(*) AS rows_on_subscriber FROM items
 rows_on_subscriber 
--------------------
               1502
(1 row)

[5441]> SELECT slot_name, active FROM pg_replication_slots
 slot_name | active 
-----------+--------
 sub       | t
(1 row)

new cluster still WITHOUT wal_level = logical: pg_upgrade --check
Performing Consistency Checks
-----------------------------
Checking for new cluster logical replication slots            
"wal_level" must be "logical" but is set to "replica"
Failure, exiting
[pg_upgrade --check exit status: 1]

### 3. set wal_level = logical and max_replication_slots on the new cluster, then upgrade
Checking for valid logical replication slots                  ok
Checking for new cluster logical replication slots            ok
Performing Upgrade
Restoring logical replication slots in the new cluster        ok
Upgrade Complete
Some statistics are not transferred by pg_upgrade.
[pg_upgrade exit status: 0]

### 4. what survived on the new publisher
[5441]> SELECT version()
                                                         version                                                          
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PostgreSQL 18.6 (Debian 18.6-1.pgdg13+2) on aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, compiled by gcc (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0, 64-bit
(1 row)

[5441]> SELECT slot_name, plugin, slot_type, active, confirmed_flush_lsn IS NOT NULL AS flushed, failover FROM pg_replication_slots
 slot_name |  plugin  | slot_type | active | flushed | failover 
-----------+----------+-----------+--------+---------+----------
 sub       | pgoutput | logical   | f      | t       | f
(1 row)

[5441]> SELECT pubname, puballtables FROM pg_publication
 pubname | puballtables 
---------+--------------
 pub     | t
(1 row)

[5441]> SELECT last_value FROM pg_sequences WHERE sequencename = 'standalone_seq'
 last_value 
------------
        506
(1 row)

the subscriber reconnects by itself (retry interval 5 s)
[5441]> SELECT slot_name, active FROM pg_replication_slots
 slot_name | active 
-----------+--------
 sub       | t
(1 row)

[5442]> SELECT count(*) AS rows_on_subscriber, max(v) FILTER (WHERE v LIKE 'after publisher%') AS last_row FROM items
 rows_on_subscriber |        last_row         
--------------------+-------------------------
               1503 | after publisher upgrade
(1 row)

[5441]> SELECT count(*) AS rows_on_publisher FROM items
 rows_on_publisher 
-------------------
              1503
(1 row)

[5442]> SELECT pid IS NOT NULL AS apply_running FROM pg_stat_subscription WHERE subname = 'sub'
 apply_running 
---------------
 t
(1 row)


